illumos: take the dma-buf (PRIME) capability from the kernel, as on Linux and
the BSDs. Without it every gallium driver reports no dma-buf import/export
on illumos; GBM then falls back to dumb buffers (XRGB scanout and ARGB
cursors only), so Xorg modesetting with glamor cannot create its ARGB8888
front buffer (ScreenInit fails) and DRI3 has nothing to share. Found with
radeonsi on amdgpu (Mac Pro 2013, illumos-drm, 2026-11-13). Upstream candidate.

--- src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_screen.c.orig
+++ src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_screen.c
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@
 
    caps->throttle = true;
 
-#if defined(HAVE_LIBDRM) && (DETECT_OS_LINUX || DETECT_OS_BSD || DETECT_OS_MANAGARM)
+#if defined(HAVE_LIBDRM) && (DETECT_OS_LINUX || DETECT_OS_BSD || DETECT_OS_MANAGARM || DETECT_OS_SOLARIS)
    if (pscreen->get_screen_fd) {
       uint64_t cap;
       int fd = pscreen->get_screen_fd(pscreen);
